name responsive
category Package
revision 69147
shortdesc Responsive design methods for LaTeX
relocated 1
longdesc Responsive design aims to display text and other design
longdesc elements well on variety of outputs, including electronic
longdesc devices or various paper sizes. It originated on the Web, using
longdesc Cascading Style Sheets to change design elements. This package
longdesc tries to achieve similar results with LaTeX. The main aim is to
longdesc support the output of multiple editions of one document with
longdesc readable font sizes regardless of the physical size of the
longdesc produced PDF, from smartphones or e-ink readers to printed A4
longdesc pages.
runfiles size=4
 RELOC/tex/latex/responsive/responsive.sty
